    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with an aggressive offensive posture, headlined by the highest-projected bat, **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Facing Will Warren, **Gunnar Henderson** leverages a massive 16% park adjustment and a 14% platoon edge to anchor the lineup. Supporting him are our primary outfield trio: **Jackson Merrill** (74.17), **Kyle Tucker** (74.09), and **Andy Pages** (71.03). **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly strong play against Robert Stock, benefiting from a high-upside matchup that offsets a minor park penalty, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start despite a mid-order slotting, thanks to his ability to exploit favorable stadium dimensions in Colorado. Furthermore, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) are primed to feast on Chris Bassitt, with both hitters seeing significant score boosts driven by high SP skill-related efficiency and advantageous platoon splits.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench centered on **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.26). While his talent profile is undeniable, his score was suppressed by a sharp -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Michael King, effectively forcing his exclusion in favor of higher-floor options like **Sam Antonacci** (61.82). The lineup remains fluid due to the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors; should **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, or **Coby Mayo** shift significantly in the batting order once official reports surface, we may see volatility in their final production. We remain cautious of **Miguel Vargas** (52.38) and **Nasim Nunez** (53.75), both of whom hover near our marginal-start threshold. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** confirmed out due to injury, the Waves must rely on high-efficiency output from the remaining core to maximize our game-cap utility across all five categories.",
